            "# Milestone 6: Model Evaluation & Refinement\n",
            "## Aircraft Engine Predictive Maintenance (AEPM) - NASA C-MAPSS FD001\n",
            "\n",
            "### 1. Target Leakage Analysis & Solution\n",
            "* **What is Target Leakage?**\n",
            "  In Milestone 4, the feature `life_percentage` was computed as:\n",
            "  $$\\text{life\\_percentage} = \\frac{\\text{current\\_cycle}}{\\text{current\\_cycle} + \\text{RUL}}$$\n",
            "  Because `RUL` (the target variable) is explicitly included in the denominator, this feature provided the model with direct knowledge of the ground-truth target. This caused artificial, inflated validation performance ($R^2 \\approx 0.996$, $\\text{RMSE} \\approx 4.01$).\n",
            "* **Why Must It Be Removed?**\n",
            "  In real production deployment, ground-truth `RUL` is unknown. Relying on `life_percentage` would cause complete failure in real-world deployment.\n",
            "* **Refinement Strategy**:\n",
            "  - Remove `life_percentage` from the feature set.\n",
            "  - Retrain `RandomForestRegressor` on the remaining 67 genuine sensor and degradation features.\n",
            "  - Generate evaluation plots (Actual vs Predicted, Residuals, Error Distribution).\n",
